network options are needed for telnet access on port 6665.","Launch QEMU in the background with the guest console exposed over localhost telnet.","Wait until the service is ready, then verify by connecting to 127.0.0.1:6665 and observing the login prompt."],"validation_strategy":["Use receipt-backed command output to confirm the process started.","Use a readiness check against localhost:6665.","Use a telnet connection to confirm the login prompt appears."],"verification_plan":["Search for relevant files and prior receipts.","Run targeted shell commands to inspect QEMU availability and launch options.","Start the VM in background.","Probe localhost:6665 until ready.","Connect via telnet and capture the prompt."],"known_bad_behavior":["Treating file existence or process launch alone as success.","Assuming readiness without a successful telnet-visible login prompt."],"evidence_gaps":["No evidence yet of the filesystem layout, QEMU availability, or the correct launch command.","No evidence yet that port 6665 is reachable or that the guest login prompt is exposed."],"risks":["QEMU may not be installed or may require a different console configuration.","The ISO may need specific boot parameters or networking setup."],"next_steps":["Inspect the environment and locate the ISO.","Check for QEMU and any helper tooling.","Launch and verify the VM service."],"finalization_evidence_required":["Receipt-backed evidence of the running QEMU process","Receipt-backed evidence of localhost:6665 readiness","Receipt-backed evidence of telnet showing the login prompt"]}}]}
